{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game narrative game narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","fileName":"Game Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Narrative","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Authored Game Narrative]] [[Emergent Game Narrative]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Authored Game Narrative","Emergent Game Narrative","Play Space","Authored Story","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game narrative game narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","fileName":"Game Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Narrative","heading":"Game Narrative","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Game narrative is a connected sequence of events made meaningful to the people involved. It can be authored directly, arise from play, or combine a fictional premise with systemic events chosen by the player.\n\nHighly prescribed narrative narrows the [[Play Space]], while a premise can scaffold interpretation without fixing one path. Systemic narrative gains authenticity from player agency but gives the designer less precise control over the resulting story.\n\nAn [[Authored Story]] is deliberately carried by the game, while an [[Emergent Story]] is the account produced through a particular act of playing. Games can combine both, letting authored context and systemic events inform how the player interprets the experience.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Authored Game Narrative","Emergent Game Narrative","Play Space","Authored Story","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game narrative game narrative","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Narrative.md","fileName":"Game Narrative.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Narrative","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Authored Game Narrative","Emergent Game Narrative","Play Space","Authored Story","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}